---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout section="OIDC" title="OpenID Connect (OIDC) Deep Dive">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="learn-layout">
      <nav class="toc">
        <div class="toc-label">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#pseudo-auth">The Pseudo-Authentication Problem</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-is">What is OpenID Connect?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#saml-vs-oidc">SAML 2.0 vs OIDC vs OAuth 2.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="#actors">OIDC Actors</a></li>
          <li><a href="#id-token">The ID Token</a></li>
          <li><a href="#scopes">OIDC Standard Scopes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#discovery">Dynamic Discovery &amp; BYOI</a></li>
          <li><a href="#execution-flow">5-Step OIDC Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#response-types">Response Types &amp; Hybrid Flow</a></li>
        </ul>
        <hr class="toc-divider" />
        <nav class="toc-nav">
          <a href={base + '/flows'}>&larr; Grant Types</a>
          <a href={base + '/tokens'}>Tokens &amp; JWT &rarr;</a>
        </nav>
      </nav>

      <main class="content">
        <div class="page-header">
          <span class="badge badge-intermediate">Intermediate &middot; 25 min</span>
          <h1>OpenID Connect (OIDC)</h1>
          <p class="lead">Understanding the identity layer on top of OAuth 2.0, solving the pseudo-authentication problem, ID Token verification, dynamic discovery, and BYOI federation.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- PSEUDO AUTH -->
        <section id="pseudo-auth">
          <h2>The Pseudo-Authentication Problem</h2>
          <p>Before OpenID Connect, developers attempted to use plain OAuth 2.0 access tokens to authenticate users. As documented by oauth.net:</p>
          <blockquote>
            "OAuth 2.0 is not an authentication protocol. Using an access token as proof of identity is like using a movie ticket as a passport: it proves you paid for a seat, but not who you are."
          </blockquote>
          
          <div class="callout warning">
            <strong>Why OAuth alone fails for authentication:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Audience Mismatch:</strong> An access token's audience (<code>aud</code>) is the API resource server, not the client application. A token issued for App A could be replayed to log into App B.</li>
              <li><strong>Opaque Formatting:</strong> Access tokens are opaque blobs to the client application.</li>
              <li><strong>No Standard Profile Schema:</strong> Different providers returned user profile data in custom, incompatible JSON shapes.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- WHAT IS -->
        <section id="what-is">
          <h2>What is OpenID Connect (OIDC Core 1.0)?</h2>
          <p>OpenID Connect combined the best parts of OAuth 2.0, Facebook Connect, and SAML 2.0 to create a lightweight identity layer on top of OAuth 2.0:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>ID Token:</strong> A cryptographically signed JWT intended specifically for the Client application.</li>
            <li><strong>UserInfo Endpoint:</strong> Standardized REST endpoint (<code>/userinfo</code>) returning validated user claims.</li>
            <li><strong>Dynamic Discovery:</strong> Metadata endpoint (<code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code>) enabling internet-scale dynamic federation.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- SAML VS OIDC -->
        <section id="saml-vs-oidc">
          <h2>SAML 2.0 vs OIDC vs OAuth 2.0</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Dimension</th><th>SAML 2.0</th><th>OAuth 2.0</th><th>OpenID Connect</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>Type</strong></td><td>Authentication / SSO</td><td>Delegated Authorization</td><td>Authentication &amp; Identity</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Token Format</strong></td><td>XML Assertion</td><td>Opaque or JWT</td><td>JSON Web Token (ID Token)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Transport</strong></td><td>HTTP POST XML</td><td>HTTPS JSON</td><td>HTTPS JSON</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Discovery</strong></td><td>Manual XML metadata exchange</td><td>None (Vendor defined)</td><td>Dynamic Discovery (JSON)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Mobile Ready</strong></td><td>Poor</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- ACTORS -->
        <section id="actors">
          <h2>OIDC Actors</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>End-User (Resource Owner):</strong> The human being whose identity is being verified.</li>
            <li><strong>Relying Party (RP / Client):</strong> The application requesting authentication.</li>
            <li><strong>OpenID Provider (OP / Authorization Server):</strong> The identity provider authenticating the user and issuing ID tokens.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- ID TOKEN -->
        <section id="id-token">
          <h2>The ID Token</h2>
          <p>A signed JWT containing identity claims for the Relying Party:</p>
          <pre><code>&#123;
  "iss": "https://authorization-server.example.com",
  "sub": "usr_998877",
  "aud": "my_client_app_id",
  "exp": 1755003600,
  "iat": 1755000000,
  "nonce": "n-0S6_WzA2Mj",
  "email": "janedoe@example.com",
  "email_verified": true
&#125;</code></pre>
          <div class="callout danger">
            <strong>Critical Rule:</strong> The ID Token is for the Client App. <strong>Never send the ID Token to backend API servers as a Bearer token!</strong> Send the Access Token instead.
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SCOPES -->
        <section id="scopes">
          <h2>OIDC Standard Scopes</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Scope</th><th>Claims Returned</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>openid</code></td><td>Required for OIDC. Returns <code>sub</code> claim.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>profile</code></td><td><code>name</code>, <code>family_name</code>, <code>given_name</code>, <code>picture</code>, <code>locale</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>email</code></td><td><code>email</code>, <code>email_verified</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>phone</code></td><td><code>phone_number</code>, <code>phone_number_verified</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>offline_access</code></td><td>Requests a Refresh Token for long-term access.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- DISCOVERY -->
        <section id="discovery">
          <h2>Dynamic Discovery &amp; BYOI (Bring Your Own Identity)</h2>
          <p>Unlike SAML's manual metadata files, OIDC enables internet-scale dynamic federation via <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code>:</p>
          <pre><code>GET /.well-known/openid-configuration HTTP/1.1
Host: accounts.example.com

<span class="c">// Response</span>
&#123;
  "issuer": "https://accounts.example.com",
  "authorization_endpoint": "https://accounts.example.com/oauth2/v1/authorize",
  "token_endpoint": "https://accounts.example.com/oauth2/v1/token",
  "userinfo_endpoint": "https://accounts.example.com/oauth2/v1/userinfo",
  "jwks_uri": "https://accounts.example.com/oauth2/v1/keys",
  "response_types_supported": ["code", "id_token", "code id_token"],
  "id_token_signing_alg_values_supported": ["RS256"]
&#125;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- EXECUTION FLOW -->
        <section id="execution-flow">
          <h2>5-Step OpenID Connect Flow</h2>
          
          <pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RP as 💻 Relying Party (App)
    participant OP as 🌐 OpenID Provider (IdP)
    participant UserInfo as 👤 UserInfo Endpoint

    Note over RP,OP: Step 1: Dynamic Discovery (BYOI)
    RP-&gt;&gt;OP: 1. GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    OP--&gt;&gt;RP: 2. Metadata (jwks_uri, auth_endpoint, token_endpoint)

    Note over RP,OP: Step 2: User Authentication &amp; Code Flow
    RP-&gt;&gt;OP: 3. GET /authorize (scope=openid profile email, nonce=n-0S6)
    OP--&gt;&gt;RP: 4. 302 Redirect with Authorization Code

    Note over RP,OP: Step 3: Token Exchange &amp; JWKS Key Fetch
    RP-&gt;&gt;OP: 5. POST /token (code, grant_type=authorization_code)
    OP--&gt;&gt;RP: 6. Tokens &#123; id_token (JWT), access_token &#125;
    RP-&gt;&gt;OP: 7. GET /.well-known/jwks.json
    OP--&gt;&gt;RP: 8. Public Verification Keys (kid, RSA Modulus, Exponent)

    Note over RP: Step 4: Local ID Token Verification<br/>Verify RS256 signature, iss, aud, exp, nonce

    Note over RP,UserInfo: Step 5: (Optional) Extended Profile Fetch
    RP-&gt;&gt;UserInfo: 9. GET /userinfo (Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;)
    UserInfo--&gt;&gt;RP: 10. 200 OK &#123; sub, name, email, picture, roles &#125;
          </pre>

          <ol>
            <li><strong>Discover Metadata:</strong> Fetch OpenID Provider configuration endpoints from <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Perform OAuth Flow:</strong> Initiate <code>/authorize</code> with <code>scope=openid profile email</code> and a cryptographic <code>nonce</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fetch JWKS Keys:</strong> Retrieve public verification keys from the published <code>jwks_uri</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Validate ID Token Locally:</strong> Check signature (RS256), issuer (<code>iss</code>), audience (<code>aud</code>), expiration (<code>exp</code>), and <code>nonce</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fetch User Profile:</strong> (Optional) Call <code>GET /userinfo</code> with the Access Token for extended profile attributes.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- RESPONSE TYPES -->
        <section id="response-types">
          <h2>OIDC Response Types &amp; Hybrid Flow</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th><code>response_type</code></th><th>Flow Category</th><th>Returned in Front Channel</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>code</code></td><td>Authorization Code Flow</td><td><code>code</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>id_token</code></td><td>Implicit Flow (Identity Only)</td><td><code>id_token</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>code id_token</code></td><td>Hybrid Flow</td><td><code>code</code>, <code>id_token</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>code id_token token</code></td><td>Hybrid Flow (Full)</td><td><code>code</code>, <code>id_token</code>, <code>access_token</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <footer class="page-footer">
          <div class="prev-next">
            <a href={base + '/flows'}>&larr; Grant Types</a>
            <a href={base + '/tokens'}>Next: Tokens &amp; JWT &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
